  "github.copilot.chat.personalInstructions": "Use a monorepo with /docs, /infra, /apps/frontend, /apps/admin, /apps/api, /packages/shared. Backend uses a single Node.js process with service modules. Use microservices only for long-running or async tasks, communicating via BullMQ or Bee-Queue. Microservices must survive external disruptions. Use Docker Compose for dev and prod, Helm charts for Kubernetes, Azure AKS with Bicep. Use ESM and npm. Express should use feature-based folders. Use Zod for validation, Prisma for Postgres, Prisma migrate only (auto-deploy on build and container restart). Use Redis for caching, queues, and recovery. Use REST-only APIs with a standard envelope { success, data, error }. Use a global error handler with Zod + envelope. Use Pino for logging unless Winston is explicitly requested. Use Zod for environment schema and keep .env.example in sync. Frontend defaults: Vite for all SPAs; Next.js allowed for business apps. Main app uses Radix + Tailwind. Admin app uses MUI. Business apps use MUI for both. Business app detection uses hybrid logic: domain keywords, folder paths, or user intent. Use atomic components, design tokens (Tailwind-first), and theme-aware components. Use Zustand only for state management. Copilot should auto-generate README updates, API docs, Mermaid diagrams, and changelogs using Conventional Commits + Keep a Changelog. Copilot should create tests as it generates code. Use Vitest with tests in /tests. Include unit tests, integration tests (Postgres test container), and mocks via vi.mock(). Always use environment variables with Zod validation. Generate secure defaults (rate limiting, CORS, helmet). Avoid over-engineering and avoid new libraries without approval. Suggest improvements and refactor legacy code to match standards. Generate GitHub Actions workflows (disabled by default), Dockerfiles, and Kubernetes manifests when relevant. Enforce semantic versioning and conventional commits. CI/CD defaults to build → test → lint → deploy, but deploy is disabled until MVP. Local dev may manually trigger deploys. Treat all rules as soft preferences.",

